course: dictionary
lesson: 1909
title: Names with a capital letter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a particular people, place or thing. These are proper nouns, and they always start with a capital letter. «The Comanche were famous as expert horse riders.» Comanche names a people, so it has a big C.
explain: One name can mean different things. Comanche can name the people, their language, or a thing named after them. The words around it are the clues: in «peoples like the Comanche became great horse riders», the clue is people, so Comanche means the people.
explain: Try the swap test. Put «a group of people» in place of Comanche in that sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found a name for a people.
fact: A proper noun is the name of a particular person, place or thing, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Comanche» means a Native American people of the southern Great Plains, today mainly in Oklahoma, USA.
fact: The Comanche were famous as expert horse riders, and their large territory was called Comanchería.
fact: «Comanche» also means the Comanche language, spoken by that people.
fact: In the Second World War, Comanche «code talkers» used their language to send secret messages for the US Army.
exercise: «The Comanche were famous as expert horse riders.» What kind of word is Comanche here? | An adjective, a describing word | A word for a kind of animal | A verb, an action word | *A proper noun, the name of a people
exercise: «Horses came back with the Spanish in the 1500s, and peoples like the Comanche became great riders.» Copy the one word that names a people. | horses | *Comanche | riders | the
exercise: Ella writes «the comanche riders were brave». Which version is correct? | the comanche riders were brave | The Comanche Riders Were Brave | the COMANCHE riders were brave | *the Comanche riders were brave
test: «The Comanche language was spoken by that people.» What does Comanche mean here? | A type of bread | A kind of horse saddle | *The language spoken by the Comanche people | A day of the week
test: Ella writes «the comanche were famous riders.» What should she change? | Remove the word the | Change riders to horse | Add a full stop at the start | *Write Comanche with a capital C
exam: «The Comanche code talkers sent secret messages for the US Army.» Which best describes what Comanche names here? | A type of gun | A word meaning secret | *A people, and their language | A kind of boat
